Subject: Re: CS1667139 - 'AECDischargeLetter' template are failing to process


Hi Josie,

Thank you for your earlier message.
As confirmed by the customer, both MESH and PDF/email outputs are affected, likely due to their shared use of the Aspose module for document conversion.
We’ve reviewed the configuration for the Discharge Medway DocX Translation action and found that both edi_exten_recip and edi_exten_sender values are non-numeric. Additionally, some entries in the database show 'PDF', which is not compliant, as EDI extensions are expected to be numeric. We raised this with the customer, who advised that this setup was originally based on guidance from Indigo4 during the initial implementation.
The customer has also indicated that the issue is specific to certain templates such as AmbulatoryCareDischargeLetter ,from the Bespoke -> DOCX_DEPARTMENT_LOOKUP table, which originate from Careflow EPR. They’ve managed to resolve some cases by rebuilding the templates, suggesting the problem may be template-specific.
To help us understand the root cause more clearly, could you please confirm how the data processing routine is handling these incoming DOCX templates? Specifically, we’re looking to understand whether the routine performs any reading, transformation, or manipulation of the document content before it is passed to the Aspose module for conversion, and what type of conversion is being carried out.

Kind regards,
____________________
 
Astha Agnihotri
Tech Support Specialist - Acute OCM Support | Optum (UK)
 
