Hi Astha

>> From reviewing the snippet, the script's purpose appears to be limited to
configuring printer settings such as paper size, print scale, and
single-sided printing and then executing the print job. It doesn't seem to
perform any other actions beyond printing.<<

EMIS' use of ScriptX has always been to set and control a browser's  print
attributes. That is what ScriptX does.

As our docs say about ScriptX.Add-On:

""In client-side HTML MeadCo's ScriptX provides full scripted control of the
printing experience within Internet Explorer including allowing a choice of
the output printer, orientation, page header and footers etc and the
initiation of printing.""

Please take a look at the questions I asked (below), such as:

"" Presumably you are using ScriptX.Add-On and are delivering the
ScriptX-enabled content to the Trust's users in Edge | IE tab ? ""

Is that a Yes or a No please?

and

""Emis / Optum has been utilising ScriptX as part of its applications across
a number of NHS Trusts for some years now, so presumably whoever wrote the
code (or someone who has a detailed working knowledge of it) is still about,
and can jump onto this thread to give us more detail.""

Same here.

In the meantime maybe somebody can jump onto a test workstation (which is
setup to be the same as the customer's boxes) and check to ensure that our
own set of samples works for you:

https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://support.meadroid.com/Developers/KnowledgeBank/HowToGuides/ScriptXAdd__;!!IqUcNYopQPk7!JNBs3epaPwKnthdVUcEaO1dhNF_WYEA7Jfra3KCBGJ_4kZEkTb3r3goDuWeanBKAeevr3xFLtBJJ5LlL9FtGmAY$
