Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-

A clear description of the Problem -
Repeat requests not reaching Winpath

Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? -

Issue started after upgrade ti Winpath.

Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) -
I reviewed the stored procedure ocs_identifyUnsentMessages, which checks the requestFinishTime field. If this field is not populated, the request will not be sent. Based on the above, Request IDs 4452866 and 4452867 are not being picked up due to their requestFinishTime being NULL.

Look to include screenshots where possible -
screenshot included

Details of the system configuration (region/organisation etc.) -
N/A

Details on the user or user type reporting the issue -
the issue affects all secondary care users

Machine specific or full hardware estate impacted e.g. Printing failure for all or one specific user/machine? -
N/A

Clinical Safety / Security / Information Governance Risk -
Yes, if users makes a repeated test the second test does not get sent which can cause delay in patient care.

Clinical Safety / Information Governance statement -
No

Workaround offered or provided – Yes / No

Order test requests separately instead of submitting them as repeat test requests.

What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge based articles have you used - 
I reviewed the stored procedure ocs_identifyUnsentMessages, which checks the requestFinishTime field. If this field is not populated, the request will not be sent. Based on the above, Request IDs 4452866 and 4452867 are not being picked up due to their requestFinishTime being NULL.

A clear set of recreation steps -
When making a test request select the option for repeat request

07/01/2026 16:04:59 - Arfan Mohammad (Work notes)
