10/12/2025 11:11:31 - Arfan Mohammad (Work notes)
Upon checking the database,

RequestID 4452863 was reportedToLims = Y.
The other two request ID 4452866 & 4452867 have set to reportedToLIM = N.

In the Sample table:

All requests are showing collected = 1  
reportedToLIMSDataeTime  for RequestID 4452863 has a date and time.
The other two request ID’s 4452866 & 4452867 are showing a NULL.

In the Request table:

Request ID 4452863 has an updated requestFinishTime.
Request IDs 4452866 and 4452867 have requestFinishTime = NULL.

I reviewed the stored procedure ocs_identifyUnsentMessages, which checks the requestFinishTime field. If this field is not populated, the request will not be sent. Based on the above, Request IDs 4452866 and 4452867 are not being picked up due to their requestFinishTime being NULL. 
Here is the relevant portion of the stored procedure for reference:


ALTER PROCEDURE [dbo].[ocs_identifyUnsentMessages]

    @imsName VARCHAR(100),

    @reTryMinutes INT = 60,

    @reTryInitDelay INT = 0,

    @reTryMaxPeriod INT = 365,

    @alternativeFlag VARCHAR(MAX) = '',

    @checkLastUpdate BIT = 0,

    @lastUpdatePeriod INT = 12

AS

    ...

    AND (CASE WHEN @checkLastUpdate = 1 THEN COALESCE(r.requestFinishTime, r.lastUpdate) ELSE r.requestFinishTime END) < DATEADD(ss, -3, GETDATE())

