"CS1677292","Spire Healthcare","2 - High","27/10/2025 09:31:48","Closed","Extracts passing EMIS/Optum validation and failing at SUS+","30/10/2025 15:59:51","system","Acute OCM Support Level 1","Astha Agnihotri","27/10/2025 17:26:59 - Astha Agnihotri (Work notes)
Hi Neil,

The reason your file passed EMIS/Optum validation but failed at SUS+ is due to configuration specific processing rules rather than a validation issue.
Optum validation accepts both 3-character and 5-character codes (e.g., NT3 or NT300) because the translation service is not bespoke to each submitter. This means the validation checks the format is valid but doesn't enforce which specific version your trust should use. It is up to the submitters, such as yourselves to ensure that when on the specification both 3 or 5 characters are accepted, you submit the correct number of characters that is appropriate to your trust. .

Please ensure that the correct identifier format is applied in future submissions to avoid similar rejections.

NT300 DOES NOT appear anywhere in the CDS 6.2. processing Routine NOR in the Sender details for Spire Healthcare Trust, so CANNOT be ""swapped"" via any CDS Translation process from NT300 to NT3, NOR visa-versa.

Regards
Astha

