13/11/2025 10:53:50 - Astha Agnihotri (Work notes)
I’ve reviewed the issue with the report for Specimen ID: B25-030599 and done some investigation. To verify the problem, I opened the file in Notepad++ and checked its structure using the View ? Summary option.
From the summary of the original file
Characters (without line endings): 9,410
Document length: 9,424
Lines: 8

This is much lower than expected because normally each HL7 segment (MSH, PID, OBR, OBX, etc.) should be on its own line, resulting in several dozen lines. Instead, the system is reading almost the entire message as one continuous line. That’s why Keystone interprets the first line as exceeding the 34,000-character limit, even though the actual file size is only about 9,400 characters.
Also, the file contains \.br\ markers instead of proper carriage return line breaks, which means the message isn’t split correctly. In short, the issue is not the overall size of the file but the formatting Hence, Keystone treats the entire message as a single unbroken line.
To confirm, I also checked a correctly processed file (screenshot attached). The summary shows:

Characters: 1,024
Lines: 125

This is the expected structure, with each segment on its own line. The difference clearly shows that the original file failed because of incorrect line breaks.

