From: Peter Moran <Peter.Moran@optum.co.uk>
Sent: 25 November 2025 09:03
To: RUPASINGHE, Ajith (EAST AND NORTH HERTFORDSHIRE NHS TRUST) <ajithrupasinghe@nhs.net>
Cc: OCM Support <ocmsupport@emishealth.com>
Subject: Re: 6.3 validate only OPA file
 
 
This message originated from outside of NHS.net Connect. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognise the sender and know the content is safe.
Ajith,
 
Can I strongly remind you that sending ""test"" files to the CDS Translation Service production environment using the Validate_Only option is strictly not allowed, as that is exactly why there is a wholly separate testing server for the testing of CDS files.
 
OPA_20251013_20251116.csv has caused the Production environment to cycle on this single file for over 16 hours - in that time there was a backlog of 14 files for 8 different customers that did not get processed.
 
The cycling of the processing of this file was due to you using the incorrect date format, which is clearly listed in the CDS v6.3 SLD specification to be CCYYMMDD.
 
The erroring field was Procedure Date, field 96, and these are two examples of your incorrect formatting -->
 
 
 
 
I have deleted the file from the Production system's processing queue.
____________________
 
Peter Moran BEng(Hons) MIET
Assoc Tech Support Analyst, OCM Support | Optum (UK)
 
Upcoming PTO: 22nd - 24th Dec, 2nd Jan 2026
 
 
 
  
