"CS1699761","The Doctors Laboratory Ltd","4 - Low","04/12/2025 17:10:40","Closed","escape tab in HL7 query","10/02/2026 12:23:14","bobbi.picton@tdlpathology.com","Acute OCM Support Level 1","Astha Agnihotri","10/12/2025 15:30:19 - Astha Agnihotri (Work notes)
Put in an escape rule into the DataRules.txt file, to escape the \X09\ to be a dash instead.
 
Or an Unescape rule

05/12/2025 15:10:08 - Astha Agnihotri (Work notes)
In HL7, \X09\ is an escape sequence representing the ASCII horizontal tab character (hex 09). HL7 uses escape sequences to include special characters in text fields without breaking the message structure.
However, when HL7 messages are parsed and displayed:
The parser converts \X09\ into an actual tab character.
Tabs are considered whitespace, not visible formatting characters.

Replace \X09\ with a visible delimiter before sending HL7
Example:
Lt ovary D1 - 18 mm
Lt ovary D2 - 10 mm

Replace with multiple spaces
Instead of \X09\, use      (four spaces) in the OBX value.

