Original case resolution

05/12/2025 13:44:54 - Ian Thompson (Work notes)
Hello Barbara,

Thank you for contacting Optum.

I have reviewed your case and have determined that this is a local issue that needs to be investigated by the online test request provider with which you are experiencing slowness.

The reason for this is once the online test request provider is selected EMIS is left and their portal opens (or pretends to open). Optum / EMIS Web support do not maintain their portal. The only configuration required within EMIS Web relating to online test requests is providing access by entering the user name and password.

The online test request provider is the organisation selected after selecting online test requests.

Unfortunately Optum / EMIS Web support do not hold the contact details for online test request providers.

To ensure the matter is resolved efficiently, we recommend raising a support request with the online test request provider with which you are experiencing slowness, providing them with the details that were originally raised.

I will now mark the case as resolved by Optum. If your local IT team deem this to be an issue related to Optum, please use the red 'Reject Solution' button and provide us with the information from your local IT team so that we are able to re investigate the issue for you.

Kind regards
Lorcan

