11/02/2026 15:45:09 - Arfan Mohammad (Work notes)
Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-

A clear description of the Problem - when a GP uses the ""Copy to Me"" feature in Review. The report is exported to Keystone, but Keystone fails validation with the error:
""Not validated – [Pathology MEDRPT v1.003 Validator Fatal] The 1st standalone test of the 1st sample has comments and/or textual results which are longer than the allowed 34,650 characters.""

This limit is defined by the PMIP specification for Pathology. While Review can accept more characters, PMIP imposes a strict limit on what can be transmitted.
In the interchange format, result text is carried in FTX+RIT lines.

Upon review of the data, there are numerous line breaks.
Each double line break is treated as a blank FTX line, and each blank line consumes one of the 99 permitted FTX lines, even though it carries no text. This means the issue is not necessarily the amount of text, but the number of required FTX lines exceeding the allowed 99 due to formatting.

Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? - The issue has always been there however they have just noticed it on 05/01/2026

Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) -

""Not validated – [Pathology MEDRPT v1.003 Validator Fatal] The 1st standalone test of the 1st sample has comments and/or textual results which are longer than the allowed 34,650 characters.""

Look to include screenshots where possible -
Screenshot are attached.

Details of the system configuration (region/organisation etc.) - N/A

Details on the user or user type reporting the issue - N/A

Machine specific or full hardware estate impacted e.g. Printing failure for all or one specific user/machine? - N/A

Details on any relevant data condition (organisation/user/patient/system) -

Review Version 1.3.0
DPR: Requested I4 Path Exporter 1.0.14
Keystone Version 1.8
DPR: indigo 4 pathology Standard 1.0.15

Clinical Safety / Security / Information Governance Risk -

