16/02/2026 17:14:43 - Astha Agnihotri (Work notes)
Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-
 
A clear description of the Problem -
Housekeeper jobs were taking significantly longer, up to 8 hours to complete, giving the impression that the process was stuck or failing. Investigation showed that the delay was caused by the Archive Directory clean?up, which had accumulated a very large backlog of files. This caused the Archive deletion task to run for many hours, delaying all subsequent Housekeeper jobs.
 
Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? -
The issue was first noticed when Housekeeper appeared to ""hang"" during its nightly run. No maintenance, upgrades or changes were being carried out at that time. The delay was due entirely to the large accumulation of archived files.
 
Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) -
Logs (as attached ss) confirmed that Housekeeper was running correctly but taking many hours to process the large Archive directory.
 
 
Look to include screenshots where possible -
Yes — screenshots were taken and attached, showing:
 
Housekeeper start times
Task durations
Archive directory file counts & size
Post?clean?up status
 
Details of the system configuration (region/organisation etc.) - Keystone environment for the The Doctors Laboratory Ltd
 
Details on the user or user type reporting the issue - Reported by Mark
 
Machine specific or full hardware estate impacted e.g. Printing failure for all or one specific user/machine? - N/A
 
Details on any relevant data condition (organisation/user/patient/system) -  Archive directory contained several days' worth of accumulated files across:
 Archive
Contents_Notes
Transit
 This backlog directly caused prolonged cleanup cycles.

Clinical Safety / Security / Information Governance Risk - No clinical or IG risk identified.
 
Clinical Safety / Information Governance statement -No patient-related or sensitive data was accessed or altered; only routine housekeeping directories were processed.
 
Workaround offered or provided –  
""The workaround is to use PowerShell scripts to manually delete the files instead of relying on Keystone to run the schedule.""
  
Have you followed all of the steps of the workaround provided on PRB - Yes
 
Does the current workaround work - Yes 
--If No selected from above state reason why not working and provide screenshots of the errors.
 
What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge based articles have you used - 
Reviewed Housekeeper logs and timestamps
Confirmed no failures in scheduled tasks
Analysed directory sizes and file counts
Completed manual deletion to restore normal processing
Consulted internal guidance regarding PowerShell?based archival clean?up
 
A clear set of recreation steps -
Allow Housekeeper to start at 01:00.
Observe the Archive Directory task — it runs first.
If a backlog exists, this task runs for several hours before any others start.
Check logs showing continuous file deletions.
Confirm other tasks do not begin until Archive cleanup completes.

