Subject: RE: issues with ECDS

 	This message originated from outside of NHS.net Connect. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognise the sender and know the content is safe. 
Hi Team,


I have pasted the below KB for you. Please complete the Phase 1 and send us the below details so that we can proceed with the account creation.
Phase 1: Set Up Your New Credentials
- Create your new BitVise User Profile.
- Send us your public key and externally facing IP address through this case.
- We'll process your key and confirm once it's ready.

PFB the KB:

>>


The CDS Translation Service is now hosted on AWS. If you already use Bitvise, you must create a new profile in your current Bitvise client to upload CDS files.
To keep things organized, start the new profile name with AWS_.
Follow the steps below to set up your new profile. 
________________________________________
Bitvise client configuration
Step 1 - Launching the Bitvise client
1.	Open Bitvise by double-clicking the desktop icon or from the Windows Programs list.
2.	The client will open with your last profile loaded.
 
3.	Click New profile on the left side.
4.	When prompted, keep profiles in the default location.
5.	Enter a name starting with AWS_ (e.g., AWS_john.smith) and click Save.
Step 2 - Host connection setup
1.	In the Host field, enter: xfer.sftp.cds-health.uk
2.	In the Port field, enter: 22
 
Step 3 - Find your external IP address
1.	
•	If using a company computer or VPN, ask your IT team for the external IP.
•	If using a personal computer, go to: https://www.whatismyipaddress.com
o	Use the IPv4 address shown.
Step 4: Generate Public / Private Key
1.	In Bitvise, go to Login tab > Client Key Manager.
2.	Click Generate New.
 
3.	Set Location and Size, then click Generate.
 
4.	Your new key will appear in the Client Key Manager.
5.	Select the new key and click Export.
 
6.	In the popup, select OpenSSH format.
7.	Click Export.
8.	Change the Save as type to Plain Text and save the file using the same name as your AWS profile.
 
Step 5 - Send Optum your Public Key
1.	Go to Cases to access your existing case.
2.	Open your case: CDS Translation Service Migration.
3.	Use the attachment option to upload your public key.
4.	Add a comment with:
•	your chosen AWS Bitvise User Profile name
•	your external IP address (e.g., 12.34.56.78)
If you receive an error, ensure the public key was saved as a .TXT file, not .PUB.
Optum will reply to your case when your setup is complete. Then proceed to Bitvise user configuration.
________________________________________
Bitvise user configuration
Step 1 - Load AWS profile
1.	Open Bitvise.
2.	Check that your new AWS profile is loaded automatically.
3.	If not, click Load Profile and select your AWS profile.
Step 2 - Enter Authentication details
1.	Go to the Login tab.
2.	Enter your new AWS Bitvise username in the Username field.
3.	For Initial method, select publickey.
4.	For Client key, select Profile 1.
 
5.	Click Save Profile.
6.	When prompted:
•	choose 'The current Windows user only' if submitting CDS files manually
•	choose 'Any account on this computer' for batch automation or SQL scripts
7.	Click OK.
 
Step 3 - Connecting to the Bitvise server
1.	Launch Bitvise.
2.	Ensure the AWS profile is loaded (use Load Profile if needed).
3.	Click Login.
4.	Bitvise will attempt to connect to the AWS SFTP server.
5.	On first login, you’ll see a prompt. Select Accept and Save.
 



Regards
Astha


