26/02/2026 13:49:03 - Peter Moran (Work notes)
I have attached 35-Char_Counts_by_Week_&_Type.txt that shows on a week by week basis the weekly counts of each of the three types of data process with counts of OK, BAD and %age BAD

26/02/2026 13:30:35 - Peter Moran (Work notes)
Used the following SQL to show counts of OK & BAD along with %_BAD for each Week and Processing type!

SELECT FORMAT(OK.t_stamp, 'dd/MM/yyyy') as ""Week\c""
	  ,OK.count_msg AS OK_msg_cnt
	  ,ISNULL(BAD.count_msg, 0) AS BAD_msg_cnt
	  ,FORMAT(ROUND(100.0 * ISNULL(BAD.count_msg, 0) / (ISNULL(BAD.count_msg, 0) + OK.count_msg), 3), '0.000') as ""% BAD""
	  ,OK.[app_name]
FROM (
	Select DATEADD(week, DATEDIFF(week, 0, l.[set]), 0) as t_stamp
		  ,Count(*) as count_msg
		  ,dpr.[app_name]  
	FROM [keystone].[dbo].[log] l with (nolock)
		JOIN [keystone].[dbo].[dpr] on dpr.dpr_id = l.dpr_id
	WHERE l.dpr_id in (13,42,61)
		AND log_type = 20
	group by DATEADD(week, DATEDIFF(week, 0, l.[set]), 0), dpr.[app_name]
	) as OK
LEFT JOIN (
	Select DATEADD(week, DATEDIFF(week, 0, l.[set]), 0) as t_stamp
		  ,Count(*) as count_msg
		  ,dpr.[app_name]  
	FROM [keystone].[dbo].[log] l with (nolock)
		JOIN [keystone].[dbo].[dpr] on dpr.dpr_id = l.dpr_id
	WHERE l.dpr_id in (13,42,61)
		AND l.[text] like '%exceeds%35%'
	group by DATEADD(week, DATEDIFF(week, 0, l.[set]), 0), dpr.[app_name]
	) as BAD
	ON OK.t_stamp = BAD.t_stamp AND OK.[app_name] = BAD.[app_name]
ORDER BY OK.t_stamp, OK.[app_name]

