11/02/2026 16:00:17 - Astha Agnihotri (Work notes)
Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-

A clear description of the Problem -

When a GP uses Review and selects the ""Copy to Me"" feature to send a report copy to EMIS Web, the file is exported from Review into Keystone.
However, when Keystone processes the message, it fails validation with the following error:
""Not validated – [Radiology NHSRSR v1.002 Validator Fatal] The patient address first line exceeds the maximum length of 35 characters.""
This occurs because the exported file does not apply the required 35?character limit to the first line of the patient address before Keystone processes it. As a result, Keystone rejects the message during validation.

Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? -
The issue has always been there however they have just noticed it on 29/01/2026


Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) -
Error Generated when file failes valisation

Not validated – [Radiology NHSRSR v1.002 Validator Fatal] The patient address first line exceeds the maximum length of 35 characters.""

What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge based articles have you used - When looking at the example message provided it clearly shows the error that the message is failing on the 35 character limit .


A clear set of recreation steps - Unable to recreate due to live system.

