"CS1752365","Homerton Healthcare NHS Foundation Trust","3 - Medium","18/03/2026 08:13:38","In Progress","The patient’s current GP practice is not updating in Review.","18/07/2026 00:17:03","system","Acute OCM Support Level 2","Peter Moran","17/07/2026 14:18:09 - Peter Moran (Work notes)
The standard structural layout for an HL7 v2.3 ADT^A31 (Update Person Information) message inbound to Cerner Millennium consists of a distinct sequence of segments. Because Cerner Millennium processes an A31 to update person-level or global demographic index profiles (rather than episode-level encounters), it heavily enforces the standard v2.3 abstract schema.

Enforced Segment Layout Hierarchy

In a standard HL7 v2.3 implementation targeting Millennium without Z-segments, the following order must be maintained: 
1.	MSH (Message Header) – Required
2.	EVN (Event Type) – Required
3.	PID (Patient Identification) – Required
4.	PD1 (Patient Additional Demographic) – Optional
5.	NK1 (Next of Kin / Associated Parties) – Optional (Repeating)
6.	PV1 (Patient Visit) – Required (Strictly for schema compliance)
7.	PV2 (Patient Visit - Additional Info) – Optional
8.	OBX (Observation / Medical Notes) – Optional (Repeating)
9.	AL1 (Patient Allergy Information) – Optional (Repeating)
10.	DG1 (Diagnosis) – Optional (Repeating)
________________________________________

Cerner Millennium v2.3 Segment Specifics

MSH – Message Header [1]
The header tells Millennium how to parse delimiters and validate message types.
•	MSH-9 (Message Type): Must be formatted exactly as ADT^A31.
•	MSH-11 (Processing ID): Expects P (Production) or D (Debugging/Test).
•	MSH-12 (Version ID): Must contain 2.3.

EVN – Event Type
•	EVN-1 (Event Trigger Code): Must be populated with A31.
•	EVN-2 (Recorded Date/Time): Format must follow the YYYYMMDDHHMMSS timestamp syntax.

PID – Patient Identification
This is the target segment used by Millennium to update core demographics across the enterprise person index.
•	PID-3 (Patient Identifier List): Must include the correct assigning authority components so Millennium can locate the exact person profile.
•	PID-5 (Patient Name): Standard v2.3 formatting requires LastName^FirstName^MiddleName^Suffix^^L (where L represents Legal).
•	PID-7 (Date/Time of Birth): Validates against historical records to prevent false matches (YYYYMMDD).

PV1 – Patient Visit (The A31 Exception)
Though the HL7 v2.3 specification marks the PV1 segment as Required for abstract structure compliance, an ADT A31 is explicitly decoupled from a real hospital visit.
•	Millennium Core Rule: Millennium expects a minimal PV1 skeleton segment.
•	Implementation Strategy: Populate PV1-2 (Patient Class) with a dummy or non-applicable character (such as N for Not Applicable or O for Outpatient) to safely bypass active encounter logic. Do not provide a specific encounter or account number in PV1-19 if you only want to affect global person fields.
________________________________________
Basic HL7 v2.3 ADT^A31 Message Example

MSH|^~\&|SENDING_SYS|SENDING_FAC|Millennium|CERNER_FAC|20260717113000||ADT^A31|MSGID987654|P|2.3
EVN|A31|20260717113000
PID|1||MRN12345^^^MRNAUTHORITY^MR||DOE^JOHN^EDWARD^^^L||19800522|M||2106-3^White^HL70005|123 MAIN STREET^^SHEFFIELD^SOUTH YORKSHIRE^S12 4XX^GBR^H||^PRN^PH^^44^114^5550199|||||||||||||||||
PV1|1|N

