29/05/2026 09:20:06 - Peter Moran (Work notes)
Reply from Chris Hill:
""
On the first point, there is a setting called ""Preferred import date"" in the import action settings, which has 3 options to pick from, these are in the screenshot below:

At the moment, NCA is set as Sample receipt date, see NCA_OCS_WinPath_Proc_Opt.png  We set this because it mirrors their Labcentre action, which they were using prior to WinPath, so when we setup the new action for Winpath, we mirrored the same import settings.

So I believe that means that where it shows the Imported date/time in Review, that is actually the Sample receipt date, not the actual date the report was imported into Review.

This setting can be changed to Date of Import instead, as above, but it will affect all Pathology being imported, not just Histopathology. Something they probably want to discuss amongst themselves, as this is setting itself mirrors the same as what it did before in Labcentre.

With the second point, based on the above, it will likely be looking in whichever field has COLDATE as the placeholder, I would have thought, in the templates, as that I think is the sample collection date/time.  Again, that can be changed too, to another place in the HL7, but as above, this affects all pathology results, not just Histopathology so would need clarifying with them what data they are sending in which fields, so we know what placeholders to use in those locations.

Frustratingly, this is what they signed off during UAT, and went live with 3 months ago...so to now be questioning that logic...makes me wonder whether they paid much attention to what it was doing.
""

Below is the OCS Pathology Template placeholder mappings of the listed dates:

MSH.6 = 202605281423 = %MSGDATE% --> PathologyMessage
ORC.9 = 202604221024
OBR.6 = 202604221023 = %RECDATE% --> Sample
OBR.7 = 202604200001 = %PERFDATE% --> Battery & %COLDATE% --> Sample
OBR.14 = 202604221024
OBR.22 = 202605281423

28/05/2026 16:44:12 - Adrian Fish (Work notes)
Pete has sent the below to the Review Developer - John Jackson

Chris & John.

Adrian and I were triaging the above case for NCA where the customer is reporting that Histopathology reports weren't showing in the date ordered list as the customer would expect.

Upon further investigation we can see a file, as attached with all PID removed, that was physically imported into review at 14:26 today (28\05\2026) where the date fields are populated as follows:

MSH.6 = 202605281423
ORC.9 = 202604221024
OBR.6 = 202604221023
OBR.7 = 202604200001
OBR.14 = 202604221024
OBR.22 = 202605281423

When I use Advanced Search within the Review GUI and search for the SampleID from the file the result is as follows, with PID removed:

Then when viewing that report it shows:

The remaining data that I've removed from the file and not shown in the last screenshot match-up perfectly!

Clearly there's a ""mix-up"" between the Import Date and the Report Date, as this report was physically imported into review at 14:26 today (28\05\2026)!

I believe from the above data that it's one of two issues:

Review is ingesting the Import and Report dates the ""wrong"" way around
The HL7 file that is being sent has the Import and Report dates incorrectly assigned

Any help \ advice would be thankfully received.

